WEBVTT

00:12:29.083 --> 00:12:30.726
Can you build on what I'm saying?

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:32.018
AG: Yeah.

00:12:32.042 --> 00:12:34.934
EP: And then sometimes I think
that you have an approach of,

00:12:34.958 --> 00:12:37.101
I agree with this, I disagree with that.

00:12:37.125 --> 00:12:41.601
And to me it's like, "Oh, is it a debate
or is it a conversation?"

00:12:41.625 --> 00:12:43.226
But I know you enough to know --

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:44.684
AG: Which do you think it is?

00:12:44.708 --> 00:12:45.976
EP: I want a conversation,

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:49.393
but because I think
when it goes into agree, disagree,

00:12:49.417 --> 00:12:52.059
I start to, you know,
if you disagree five times,

00:12:52.083 --> 00:12:54.268
then I'm going to want to
prove myself to you.

00:12:54.292 --> 00:12:57.309
And then I feel that you have, you know,
I want your approval.

00:12:57.333 --> 00:13:00.643
I prove myself to someone
from whom I want your approval.